{"step_index":1489,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:55:54Z","input_tokens":2565,"cache_read_tokens":124649,"output_tokens":408,"thinking":"Bybit's REST API lacks CORS headers, potentially blocking browser-based direct `fetch()` requests to the testnet endpoint. However, Bybit's WebSocket endpoints are CORS-free. WebSockets provide a viable method for streaming live updates from any browser origin.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"bun -e '\nconst ws = new WebSocket(\"wss://stream-testnet.bybit.com/v5/public/linear\");\nws.onopen = () => {\n  console.log(\"Connected to Bybit Testnet WS!\");\n  ws.send(JSON.stringify({ op: \"subscribe\", args: [\"tickers.BTCUSDT\", \"orderbook.1.BTCUSDT\"] }));\n};\nws.onmessage = (e) => {\n  console.log(\"Got Bybit Message:\", e.data.slice(0, 150));\n  ws.close();\n  process.exit(0);\n};\nws.onerror = (err) => {\n  console.error(\"WS error:\", err);\n  process.exit(1);\n};\nsetTimeout(() => process.exit(0), 4000);\n'","Cwd":"/Users/dev/Documents/Antigravity/grok-bot-dashboard","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing Bybit testnet WebSocket","toolSummary":"Test Bybit WebSocket"}}]}
